# Prismic slices

## Settings

Every slice has a `settings` group: `padding_top`, `padding_bottom`, `theme`.
Pass them to the Lumos `Section` that wraps the slice.

Theme options: `inherit`, `light`, `dark`, `brand`. Default is always
`inherit` in the model (`theme.default_value`) and in code:

```tsx
theme={slice.primary.settings?.theme ?? "inherit"}
```

Never fall back to `dark`, `light`, or `brand`. Set an explicit theme only
when the design asks for it.

## CSS

No CSS in the slice React file: no `Styles` helper, no `const css = \`...\``.
Put styles in `src/slices/<Name>/index.css` under `@layer components`, and
import at the top of `index.tsx`:

```tsx
import "./index.css";
```

The `Styles` helper stays for library components under `src/components/` only.
A DOM script or browser state stays in the same `index.tsx` when the slice is
a Client Component (`"use client"`).

## Screenshots

After building or changing a slice visually, capture
`src/slices/<Name>/screenshot-default.png` from the local site. Crop roughly
one viewport of the section (~1280 × 800–900), not an entire sticky scroll
track. That file is the equivalent of Slice Machine’s “Update screenshots”
when that button is not usable.

## Content

Fill the section’s Prismic content (copy, links, images, settings) in the same
pass as the model and component. Publish after writing. See
`.agents/skills/lumos-prismic/SKILL.md`.
